# AC Widget — optional environment configuration.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in what you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# ".env" is listed in .gitignore and must never be committed.
#
# You do NOT need this file for normal use. `bash setup.sh` stores credentials
# in the macOS Keychain, which is the recommended place for them. Use .env when
# you are developing, running on a machine without a Keychain, or keeping
# secrets in your own secret manager.
#
# Precedence: variables already set in the shell win, then this file, then the
# Keychain.

# --- Which air conditioner -------------------------------------------------
# Overrides the brand recorded in config.json by `setup.sh`.
# Registered ids: miraie, demo
#AC_BRAND=miraie

# --- Brand credentials -----------------------------------------------------
# Pattern: AC_<BRAND-ID>_<FIELD-NAME>, both upper case. Each driver declares
# its own fields; run `python -c "import acbrands,json;
# print(json.dumps(acbrands.catalogue(), indent=2))"` to list them.
#
# Panasonic MirAIe:
#AC_MIRAIE_MOBILE=+910000000000
#AC_MIRAIE_PASSWORD=your-miraie-password

# --- TV / home network access ----------------------------------------------
# Serves the same controls on the local network, guarded by a shared token.
# Leave both unset to keep the app loopback-only.
# Generate a token with: openssl rand -hex 16
#AC_LAN_PORT=8765
#AC_LAN_TOKEN=replace-with-a-random-32-character-token

# --- Development helpers ---------------------------------------------------
# Swap which unit is treated as the bedroom and which as the hall.
#AC_SWAP_ROOMS=1
# Demo brand only: "minimal" renders a deliberately plain unit, to check that
# the panel hides controls the AC does not support.
#AC_DEMO_CAPS=minimal
